01:24:02,912 --> 01:24:05,956
- Maybe we should drop it all.
-No.

752
01:24:06,833 --> 01:24:09,376
<i>The Reds' coach asks for a timeout ...</i>

753
01:24:09,461 --> 01:24:12,129
<i>and trying to get his players out.</i>

754
01:24:12,213 --> 01:24:14,339
Off the track! You must go off the field.

755
01:24:14,424 --> 01:24:16,300
She should kill herself.

756
01:24:16,384 --> 01:24:19,470
No. She's right. Get off the field.

757
01:24:28,229 --> 01:24:29,730
Will someone stop this?

758
01:24:30,065 --> 01:24:33,275
- We should interrupt the broadcast.
-No. Drop it.

759
01:24:34,569 --> 01:24:38,238
Off the track, Katya. Denekin, out with you.

760
01:24:39,532 --> 01:24:40,949
Stupid cowboy.

761
01:24:44,788 --> 01:24:46,789
You don't need to continue.

762
01:24:51,086 --> 01:24:53,170
The man wants to see a show, Rid.

763
01:24:53,880 --> 01:24:56,006
We better show him one.

764
01:25:15,360 --> 01:25:16,527
Red!

765
01:25:45,306 --> 01:25:47,141
Back on the field!

766
01:25:59,070 --> 01:26:00,904
Disconnect the satellite connection.

767
01:26:01,573 --> 01:26:02,906
Cut it off!

768
01:26:10,331 --> 01:26:12,040
Then that's enough!

769
01:26:18,047 --> 01:26:21,550
Don't you understand? They kill him...

770
01:26:23,136 --> 01:26:24,887
to increase viewership!

771
01:26:44,866 --> 01:26:46,325
It's not in the script!

772
01:26:46,409 --> 01:26:47,409
Hello!

773
01:26:47,577 --> 01:26:48,744
Sit down!

774
01:26:48,912 --> 01:26:51,955
Open your eyes though, fool.
The world is going downhill.

775
01:26:52,207 --> 01:26:54,625
Can't you hear? Sit down!

776
01:26:54,709 --> 01:26:55,876
Clean me up.

777
01:26:57,378 --> 01:27:00,172
You don't control us anymore.

778
01:27:05,553 --> 01:27:07,137
Jonathan.

779
01:27:34,332 --> 01:27:35,999
Hear the audience.

780
01:27:45,927 --> 01:27:48,053
I better get this figured out.

781
01:28:44,652 --> 01:28:45,819
Then score.

782
01:28:48,573 --> 01:28:49,656
Then score!

783
01:28:53,286 --> 01:28:55,245
Shut up!

784
01:29:28,696 --> 01:29:29,821
Come on!

785
01:30:46,732 --> 01:30:49,484
Well done. What a great show.

786
01:30:50,153 --> 01:30:52,446
I wonder what he was looking for.

787
01:30:54,782 --> 01:30:56,408
Surely these.

788
01:31:00,121 --> 01:31:02,080
Well, young Jonathan…

789
01:31:03,040 --> 01:31:05,208
you have done excellently.

790
01:31:05,293 --> 01:31:07,669
One of the basic rules of this kind is,

791
01:31:07,753 --> 01:31:10,464
that one must never kill a tyrant...

792
01:31:11,132 --> 01:31:14,468
without having planned anything
with his successor.

793
01:31:15,845 --> 01:31:18,305
You understand that, right?

794
01:31:18,931 --> 01:31:22,267
Yes. That means I'm not done yet.

795
01:31:44,749 --> 01:31:47,083
Maybe this fight is over.

796
01:32:19,700 --> 01:32:21,868
Hi, it's me. It's me.

797
01:32:27,208 --> 01:32:30,085
Maybe you've started a revolution.

798
01:32:31,003 --> 01:32:33,255
Get those hailstones out.

799
01:32:33,339 --> 01:32:36,675
- No, he shot past.
-Not quite.

800
01:32:45,393 --> 01:32:46,851
What are they doing?

801
01:32:46,936 --> 01:32:50,272
You confronted one of the monsters,
that govern their lives.

802
01:32:51,023 --> 01:32:53,024
And they saw you do it.

803
01:33:00,116 --> 01:33:03,076
-Where are we going?
-First we have to go to the doctor.

804
01:33:03,160 --> 01:33:04,953
And if you can handle it…

805
01:33:05,538 --> 01:33:08,164
I will take you home
in my bed afterwards.

806
01:33:11,252 --> 01:33:13,253
Translation city
Sheila Hasahya


